* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call !tkpickrec(ctx, mode, file, id, res, newtext)       ALWAYS SIX ARGUMENTS: a call with fewer stops with "Argument count mismatch" (pad with '')
*
*   As $tk_pickrec: mode null picks a file and then a record in it, 'file' only a file, 'record' a record of the file given, 'list' one entry of a list the program gives.
*   THE PICKER NEVER WRITES: it opens a file for reading, takes no lock and changes nothing.  It opens the files the account's own VOC names, by the account's own rights.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine tkpickrec(ctx, mode, file, id, res, newtext)
$catalog !tkpickrec

   call $tk_pickrec(ctx, mode, file, id, res, newtext)
   return
end

* END-CODE
